    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Win the 'Game' pot by having the lowest points or going out, and win the 'Flip/Flop' pots by holding low cards.",
      "Turn-flow example: 1. Players reveal cards to claim Flip/Flop pots immediately.\n2. Standard Draw/Discard Rummy play ensues.\n3. Melds: Sets (3+ of a kind) or Runs (3+ sequential in suit).\n4. Dropping: At the start of your turn, you can place your cards face-up to 'Drop' (Knock). If you have the lowest point total, you win the Game Pot. If someone has lower/equal, you lose double ('Caught').",
      'Scoring example: Three-pot betting system: game pot, flip pot, and flop pot with claims based on the original dealt cards. Flip pot goes to lowest card in flip suit; flop pot goes to lowest card in the other suit of same color if present. Game pot is won by valid drop, tunk out, or lowest hand when stock ends; double-game-pot outcomes apply for 50, tunk out, and caught drops..',
